<h2>5.2 Service Category Analysis</h2>
<p>Analyzing expenditure by service category shows that compute virtual machines represent the largest single expense category (52.4%), followed by managed relational and NoSQL databases (23.8%), block and object storage (14.2%), and cross-region network egress (9.6%). Network egress exhibited the highest coefficient of variation (CV = 1.42), indicating that data transfer fees are the most unpredictable cost category in multi-cloud deployments.</p>

