<h2>5.3 Machine Learning Evaluation & Confusion Matrix</h2>
<p>The anomaly detection model was tested against 32,850 ground-truth records containing 603 verified cost anomalies (such as runaway load tests, accidental GPU spin-ups, and unattached volume leaks). The confusion matrix yielded: True Negatives (TN) = 32,187, False Positives (FP) = 60, False Negatives (FN) = 20, and True Positives (TP) = 583.</p>

